Recorded in CLAUDE.md because the planner reads this file as required input on
every plan generation. A goal that lives only in a chat log does not reach the
autonomous loop, which is planning milestones on its own right now.

The directive has two clauses and the second is the harder one. Replicating
AVO's result with Qwen3.8-27B in place of Claude is the visible half. The other
half -- "how their harness iterated its own autogenerated way to finding this
success on its own" -- is the self-directed search method, and the transferable
question it poses is what the harness did WHEN IT DID NOT KNOW WHAT TO DO NEXT.
An architecture diagram without that mechanism misses the point.

Why this is not just another ARC rule. Our public-set score is already 183/183,
the same as AVO's, but ours came with 25 hand-built per-game adapters and theirs
came with none. The gap is transfer to a hidden game, which is the whole
deliverable. The reported 100%-vs-30% split between harness and bare model is
this project's own thesis stated as a measurement.

The entry records the known blocking prerequisite rather than leaving it to be
rediscovered: agent-as-mutation-operator needs tool calls, and the scored vLLM
server returns HTTP 400 on any request carrying tools. Every AVO number is
marked secondary-source until confirmed against NVIDIA's own writeup, because
the coverage 403s on direct fetch.

